# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is written on the assumption that every file and every commit
# may eventually become publicly visible. Anything that could carry a secret,
# a credential, customer data or internal infrastructure detail is ignored here.
# See docs/public-release-checklist.md before changing repository visibility.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets and credentials (never commit) --------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.truststore
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*.ppk
credentials
.credentials
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
secrets.json
*secret*.yaml
*secret*.yml
!**/templates/*secret*.yaml
local-dev-keys/
.aws/
.kube/
kubeconfig
kubeconfig.*
*.kubeconfig

# --- Terraform --------------------------------------------------------------
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl.bak

# Provider lock files belong to the ROOT modules that own the provider
# requirements -- the environments -- and are committed there, pinned for every
# platform CI runs on. A lock file inside a reusable module is an artifact of
# validating it standalone: the module does not choose the provider version, its
# caller does, so committing one there would pin a version the caller never
# asked for.
infrastructure/terraform/modules/*/.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.*
plan.out
plan.json
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
.terraformrc
terraform.rc
*.auto.tfvars
terraform.tfvars
!terraform.tfvars.example
!*.auto.tfvars.example

# --- Java / Maven -----------------------------------------------------------
target/
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
*.class
*.jar
*.war
*.ear
*.nar
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*
.flattened-pom.xml
dependency-reduced-pom.xml

